# React Standards

- Use functional components only.
- Prefer hooks over class components.
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Avoid overly large components.

## Components

- Separate presentation from business logic when complexity grows.
- Avoid deeply nested JSX.
- Extract reusable pieces when reuse is expected.
- Prefer explicit props over implicit behavior.

## State

- Use local state for local concerns.
- Extract reusable stateful logic into custom hooks.
- Avoid unnecessary global state.
- Avoid duplicated derived state.

## Rendering

- Prevent unnecessary re-renders when relevant.
- Use memoization only when justified.
- Avoid creating unstable objects/functions unnecessarily inside render.

## Effects

- Keep useEffect predictable and minimal.
- Avoid effects that synchronize unnecessary state.
- Cleanup subscriptions and listeners properly.

## Routing

- Keep route components lightweight.
- Move business logic outside routing definitions when possible.